#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: rust-serve-dies-permanently-after-one-handler-panic
description: "one panic in one handler poisons the http runtime mutex, so a served program answers NOTHING afterwards while its process stays up"
---
# One handler panic and the server never answers again (rust lane)

Reported from rozum. A handler read a `.jsonl` file line by line and passed each line to
`jsonParse`. The file's last line was empty — every file written by appending has one — so
`jsonParse` aborted the thread. That much is arguably fine.

What is not: the process **stayed up and stopped answering everything**, for good. The log shows
one panic followed by an unbounded run of

```text
thread 'tokio-rt-worker' panicked at src/runtime/http.rs:224:37:
called `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` value: PoisonError { .. }
```

Every later request on that server — including requests to unrelated routes — fails the same way.
From outside the service is listening and returning nothing, which is the hardest failure to
diagnose: healthy port, healthy process, no answers.

Two things would each be enough on their own:

1. **A handler panic must not take the server with it.** Catch it at the route boundary and answer
   500, or do not hold a lock across handler execution — a poisoned mutex makes one bad request
   permanent rather than momentary.
2. **A fallible JSON parse.** There is no `jsonParse` spelling that returns `Option`/`Either`, so a
   server handling input it did not write has no way to refuse it. The reporter's workaround is to
   inspect the text first and only hand `jsonParse` something starting with `{` or `[`, which
   cannot be right for arbitrary input.

To see it: build this, run it, then

```sh
curl -s localhost:8431/ok            # alive
curl -s localhost:8431/boom          # nothing — the handler panicked
curl -s localhost:8431/ok            # nothing, and never again
```

```scalascript
[route, serve, Request, Response](std/http.ssc)
[jsonParse](std/json.ssc)

val TEXT: Map[String, String] = Map("Content-Type" -> "text/plain")

def okRoute(req: Request): Response =
  Response(200, TEXT, "alive")

// The whole of the defect: ONE handler that panics on input it did not write.
def boomRoute(req: Request): Response =
  val v = jsonParse("")
  Response(200, TEXT, "never reached")

def main(): Unit =
  route("GET", "/ok", r => okRoute(r))
  route("GET", "/boom", r => boomRoute(r))
  serve(8431)
```
